{
  "_comment": [
    "Single source of truth for the LiteLLM model registry. Consumed by",
    "scripts/sync-models-to-db.sh (POST /model/new) and scripts/set-model-costs.sh",
    "(POST /model/update). Each entry is a literal /model/new payload.",
    "",
    "Cost fields live in litellm_params, NOT model_info: /model/update only",
    "persists litellm_params (it reads model_info purely to resolve model_info.id),",
    "so litellm_params is the only placement that works for both endpoints.",
    "LiteLLM's router copies every CustomPricingLiteLLMParams field out of",
    "litellm_params into the model cost map at load time, so cost tracking picks",
    "them up either way. Floats skip the litellm_params encryption path, so these",
    "stay readable as plain JSON numbers in Postgres.",
    "",
    "Costs are USD per token = (USD per 1M tokens) / 1e6. These are reference",
    "market rates for the equivalent hosted model, not our GPU cost — see",
    "docs/model-pricing.md for the per-model source and how to refresh."
  ],
